# Coding Standards

Reference: `docs/DEVELOPMENT_GUIDE.md`

Language and style only.

## TypeScript

- Strong typing everywhere. Avoid `any`. Prefer explicit domain types.
- Prefer readable, explicit code over clever abstractions.
- Meaningful names over comments. Comments explain why, not what.

## React

- Functional components only.
- Extract reusable logic into hooks.
- Keep components small; one responsibility per file.
- Do not add `useMemo` / `useCallback` by default.

## Naming

- Components: `PascalCase.tsx`
- Hooks / utils: `camelCase.ts`
- Folders: `kebab-case`
- Prefer purpose names: `CreateSale`, `InventoryAdjustment`, `ReceiptPreview`
- Never ship `Temp`, `Data2`, `HelperNew`, `Final`

## Imports

- Respect folder ownership and dependency direction.
- No circular imports.
- Colocate feature code inside the feature.

## Quality bar

Simple > clever. Explicit > implicit. Reuse > duplicate. Small modules > large files.
